      "mammal_tmax_predicted_for_30kg_years": 24.424791718266466,
      "kleiber_metabolic_exponent": 0.75,
      "explanation": "Across species, lifespan exponent ~+0.15 to +0.19 (de Magalhaes 2007). Within dogs, ~-0.1. Both hold because they are slopes of different relationships: ln T_ij = alpha + beta_between*ln M_j + beta_within*(ln M_ij - ln M_j). beta_between reflects evolved maintenance (large species evolved slower aging, b_species ~ M^-beta). beta_within reflects recent artificial selection for size via growth pathways (IGF-1) without time to evolve matching maintenance; here b rises with mass."
    }
